.TH DANBY-FLYBALL 1
.SH NAME
danby-flyball \- flight of a batted baseball
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/flyball
.SH MODEL
A ball launched one metre above the ground is acted on by gravity, quadratic
drag, and backspin-induced Magnus lift.  Integration ends at an interpolated
ground crossing, allowing range and hang time to be read without timestep
quantization.
.SH DISPLAY
The spatial plot shows the complete arc and the telemetry plot shows speed.
Tracks alter exit speed, angle, drag, lift, backspin, and gravity.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/flyball.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR trajectory (2)
